# The PowerVR GX6250 is a render-only GPU (no display outputs). Mutter must
# not try to adopt its card node as a secondary GPU: when it does, its cogl
# buffer handling starts failing (cogl_buffer_impl_gl_map_range assertions,
# "Failed to lock front buffer on /dev/dri/card1"), and the next screen fade
# kills the frame clock ("clutter_frame_clock_notify_ready: code should not
# be reached"), leaving the panel permanently black with the backlight off.
# Verified on hardware 2026-08-30: the first cogl failure landed five
# seconds after the powervr driver bound. Vulkan clients open the render
# node (/dev/dri/renderD128) directly; hiding the card node from mutter
# costs nothing.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card*", DRIVERS=="powervr", ENV{MUTTER_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
